course: dictionary
lesson: 11706
title: A new word in context: auditorium
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name places. When you meet a new one, look at the words around it for clues. «The head teacher walked into the auditorium and the whole school went quiet.» A head teacher is speaking to a whole school, so an auditorium must be a big place where many people gather.
explain: «The auditorium was packed, so the late children had to stand at the back.» Packed means full, and standing at the back means there were no seats left. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A room, a hall or a theatre might fit, so the clues point to a place where an audience sits.
explain: Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. «The Christmas concert was held in the school auditorium.» If you swap in "the large school hall where people sit to watch", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: An auditorium is a large room or building where an audience sits to watch a play, concert or talk.
fact: In a theatre, the auditorium is the part where the audience sits.
fact: Schools often use the auditorium, or school hall, for assemblies, concerts and plays.
fact: The plural of auditorium can be auditoriums or auditoria.
fact: A packed auditorium is one with almost no empty seats.
exercise: «The school auditorium was full for the Christmas concert.» What is an auditorium? | *A large room where an audience sits to watch a show | A type of bus used on school trips | A small kitchen for cooking lunches | A playground with swings
exercise: In maths, an auditorium has 20 rows of 30 seats. How many seats are there in total? | 50 | 620 | 500 | *600
exercise: «Every seat in the auditorium was taken, so the late children stood at the back.» What does this tell you about the auditorium? | It was closed for repairs | *It was packed with people | It was very small | It was empty
test: The head teacher spoke to the whole school in the auditorium. Where did the head teacher speak? | A forest | A kitchen | A bus | *A large hall where people sit to listen
test: Which phrase describes an auditorium with no empty seats? | A glum playground | *A packed auditorium | A curt reply | A treacherous path
exam: Which words best describe what an auditorium is? | A park with trees and benches | A room for cooking and eating | A shop that sells tickets for buses | *A large place where an audience sits to watch a play, concert or talk
